Definition of a fallen angel right here. This game use to be my bread and butter of gaming but over the years, the community was split because the♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥decisions the developers made. Every yearly patch that they did tried to make the game play the way they wanted it to be played rather than how the community played the game. The game is nothing more than a walk down hallway to do objective A and backtrack to B to wait for C kind of game. I have nothing against those games but the fact that it didn't start that way rustled my jimmies. If you want a more skill based competitive zombie game, you're looking in the wrong area... The problem is that there is no other competitive game like it...
-Here's a small edit;
After 3 years (since this crappy review was wrote), I promised a friend that I would go back and play a few rounds just for old time sake. Well, my review holds the testament of time. That "split community" has basically evaporated to <50 players total with bots making up the majority. Jimmies are still rustled.

Pros:
- The game so far has been running smoothly (saw some people complaining about crashes but never experienced it yet, so it might have been fixed);
- The theme is amazing and the playable classes have really interesting abilities that result in fun sinergies with the items;
- Has a funny artifact forging system that makes scavenging rewarding, also items gathered beyond their limit get recycled into resouces for forging (although recipes seem somewhat rare);
- The devs continue to update the game and gives us more content.
Cons:
- The use of your second/third abilites is horrible, don't know if the devs plan to change it later but they should. As it is now they tell you early on E and Q are for your second/third abilities, but this just changes the ability you can use from the second to the third and vice-versa. Meaning if you want to use them in rapid sucession you click the right mouse button, change the ability with Q or E and then RMB again. Why can't we just have a button that does the other abilty automatically?
- Some early enemies (by what I've seen so far) have dangerous spawning... literally. Both the ghosts and black cyclops on the first stage will sometimes simply phase on top of you and, since they damage you by simply go agains't you, you can see how this can be somewhat infuriating;
- It's dangerous to explore... and no, I don't mean because of the Redeemer. Enemies continuously spawn in the map and they might spawn near you in a previously cleared room only to surround you and end your run. Sure the game provides you with the tools to deal with this on the squishier classes but then we go back to the first con;
- Some ranged enemies can shoot you from off-screen. I don't think it's an awful thing but it might turn some people off if their runs end due to this.
Summary:
The game has an awesome concept and great replayability due to the great variety of classes and items but the cons I posted might turn people off and keep the game from getting the appreciation I believe it deserves, because it really is that fun! Also, at least in my opinion, I don't think the cons I posted are that difficult to fix and would greatly improve the gameplay. Still recommending it though, since the devs keep updating the game I have hope they might fix this in the future.

